# Build context exclusions for the production API image.
#
# Céluma 1.3 Phase 2 closure: the runtime image ships application code,
# `alembic/` (start.sh runs `alembic upgrade head` on boot) and `start.sh`.
# Nothing else — no tests, no docs, no coverage output, no local artifacts.
# See docs/celuma-1.3/phase-2-closure/backend-image-size-analysis.md.

# VCS
.git
.gitignore
.github/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Tests and test tooling — never part of the runtime image.
# `requirements-dev.txt` is NOT excluded: the `dev` build target installs from
# it. It is a ~400-byte manifest; the packages it names are never installed
# into the `runtime` target.
tests/
pytest.ini
run_tests.py
.pytest_cache/

# Coverage / test outputs
htmlcov/
.coverage*
coverage.xml

# Documentation — the image serves an API, not Markdown.
docs/
*.md

# Local database dumps and scratch state
backups/
.oldchain/

# IDE / project files
.idea/
.vscode/
.cursor/
*.code-workspace

# Build artifacts
build/
dist/

# Local orchestration — the image is built from this context, never runs it
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Misc
.env
.env.*
*.log
.DS_Store
